  nonce: 3eaa  # 3eaa
  message: "Done in PR #2176 (commit 0ed1014868). Read from tier files written by the new code (`hypergumbo survey --out`), every metrics figure checked against the tier's own arrays and the full survey beside it (script: lokuj-read.py; 10 checks per file, 9 files, all hold):\n  alertmanager 4k/16k/64k: nodes 7/43/218; by_supply_chain_tier was {'unknown': 7/43/218}, is {'first_party': 7/43/218}; languages was {'go': 0, 'unknown': 0} (files), is {'go': 7} (nodes) with no files key.\n  killbill 4k/16k/64k: nodes 3/38/183; {'unknown'} -> {'first_party'}.\n  kserve 4k/16k/64k: nodes 4/35/163; {'unknown'} -> {'first_party'}; 64k languages {'go': 65, 'python': 98}.\nA THIRD INSTANCE OF THE MECHANISM, found while verifying: a node with no language of its own (a route marker) was counted under a language \"unknown\" the full map does not have, because the slim node drops discovery_language. Fixed by the same change.\nWHAT A VIEW'S METRICS NOW ARE: computed from the selected Symbols' full records; languages.<lang>.files and debug absent (never zero); the one repository figure under metrics.repository.framework_patterns; a source without that count gives no key. The test file test_view_metrics.py reads every figure of a view's metrics on a three-language, three-tier fixture (tiered at two budgets, compact in both selection modes) and fails on a figure it has no rule for. Eight mutations each turned a test red.\nLIMIT OF THE REAL-FILE EVIDENCE: every node those nine tier files selected is first-party, so the real files show one tier; the multi-tier case is shown by the fixture only.\nALSO CORRECTED in the spec: total_files is the distinct node-path count (INV-mozaf), not the sum over profile.languages.\nNOT CHANGED, by ruling (WI-zafid): analysis_incomplete: false beside limits.partial_results_reason."  # 3eaa
